# Pull requests

`.github/workflows/pr-template-check.yml` fails the PR if any of this is missing. It re-runs when the title or description is edited.

## Title

Conventional commit: `type(scope): summary`, lowercase type, no trailing period.
Types: `feat fix docs style refactor perf test build ci chore revert`.

## Description

Start from `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` and keep every heading. Pass the body with `gh pr create --body-file <file>` so markdown is not mangled.

- **Checklist**: tick only what is true. "All new and existing tests passed" means `composer check:full` passed on the pushed head.
- **Types of changes**: tick every type present in the commits; the title's type must be ticked.
- **Description**: what the PR does and why, for a reviewer who has not seen the conversation. Link docs instead of repeating them.
- **Commits**: a table with one row per commit (or group of related commits), `| Commit | What |`. Use the conventional prefix as the commit label.
- **Behavior changes**: every runtime difference a user or consumer app can notice: bug fixes (old vs new behavior), changed defaults, removed or renamed options, new side effects, migrations. Write `None` only if nothing changes at runtime.
- **Related Issue**: link it, or leave the section empty.

## After opening

- Open as draft until CI is green.
- The quality report comment is posted by CI (`bin/quality-report`); do not post it by hand.
- When new commits change behavior, update the Commits and Behavior changes sections in the same push.
